message.content:
{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "All new library functions will be added to the existing Fabric configtxutil package to align with existing codebase conventions and reuse existing config parsing, traversal, and ConfigUpdate computation utilities.",
    "Capability modification functions will use explicit toggle-style methods (e.g., EnableV20ApplicationCapability(), DisableV20ApplicationCapability()) instead of allowing arbitrary capability value setting, to prevent invalid capability configurations that would cause channel update failures.",
    "All new functions will follow existing Fabric error handling patterns, returning descriptive errors for invalid inputs (e.g., non-existent orderer endpoints, invalid org types, unsupported ACL names) to improve usability for Fabric administrators.",
    "Example tests will be split into separate, focused test functions per U8 requirements, instead of modifying the existing single end-to-end config update test, to make examples easier to understand and reuse.",
    "The generic organization policy retrieval function will support all Fabric org types (application, orderer, consortium) by leveraging existing config group traversal logic, avoiding duplicate code for each org type."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The existing configtxutil package has stable, production-ready utilities for parsing config blocks, traversing config groups, and computing valid ConfigUpdate transactions, so new functions will build on these existing utilities rather than reimplementing core logic.",
    "The development environment (Go toolchain, Fabric test harness, existing test fixtures for sample channel configs and org MSP definitions) is already set up and available, so no effort is allocated for environment setup or baseline fixture creation.",
    "All new functionality will be compatible with the latest stable Hyperledger Fabric release (v2.5) and will not require changes to core Fabric consensus, membership, or peer services.",
    "Code review, merge, and external documentation update effort is excluded from this estimate, as the scope is limited to development and unit/integration test implementation.",
    "Existing unit test patterns and mock utilities for config transactions are available for use, so no effort is needed to create new test infrastructure."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Implement orderer endpoint addition function",
      "activity_description": "Develop, unit test, and validate the library function to add an orderer endpoint to an orderer org's config group, including input validation for config block structure, endpoint format validation, and integration with existing ConfigUpdate computation logic to meet U1 acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement orderer endpoint removal function",
      "activity_description": "Develop, unit test, and validate the library function to remove an orderer endpoint from an orderer org's config group, including validation for endpoint existence, error handling for non-existent endpoints, and integration with ConfigUpdate computation to meet U2 acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement organization policy retrieval helper",
      "activity_description": "Develop the generic reusable function to retrieve all policies for a specified org (application, orderer, consortium) from a config transaction, leveraging existing config group traversal utilities, with unit tests for all org types to meet U3 acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement capabilities retrieval helper",
      "activity_description": "Develop the function to extract orderer, application, and channel capabilities from a config transaction, returning a structured config.Capabilities object, with validation for missing capability groups and unit tests to meet U4 acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Implement capability modification functions",
      "activity_description": "Develop toggle-style Enable/Disable functions for application, orderer, and channel capabilities, including validation to prevent setting unsupported capabilities, and unit tests for all capability types and input scenarios to meet U5 acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Implement application configuration retrieval helper",
      "activity_description": "Develop the function to extract the full application configuration (including org definitions, ACLs, capabilities) from a config transaction and return a structured config.Application object, with unit tests for valid and invalid config scenarios to meet U6 acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Implement application ACL modification functions",
      "activity_description": "Develop functions to add and remove ACLs from an application group's policy configuration, including validation for valid ACL names and policy types, integration with ConfigUpdate computation, and unit tests to meet U7 acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Implement orderer configuration update example test",
      "activity_description": "Create a separate, focused example test demonstrating how to update orderer configuration (including orderer policies) and retrieve organization policies using the new library functions, with clear comments and valid test fixtures to meet U8 and U3 requirements.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Implement application configuration update example test",
      "activity_description": "Create a separate, focused example test demonstrating how to update application-specific values (including application policies and ACLs) using the new library functions, with clear comments and valid test fixtures to meet U8 and U7 requirements.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Implement organization management update example test",
      "activity_description": "Create a separate example test demonstrating how to add/remove orgs, update anchor peers for application orgs, and add/remove orderer endpoints for orderer orgs using the new library functions, to meet U8, U1, and U2 requirements.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Implement MSP modification example test",
      "activity_description": "Create a separate example test demonstrating how to modify organization MSP definitions using existing and new library functions, with clear comments and valid test fixtures to meet U8 requirements.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Implement capabilities update example test",
      "activity_description": "Create a separate example test demonstrating how to add, remove, enable, and disable application, orderer, and channel capabilities using the new library functions, to meet U8 and U5 requirements.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "Integration testing of new functionality",
      "activity_description": "Execute end-to-end integration tests to verify that all new config modification functions produce valid ConfigUpdate transactions compatible with Fabric's signature workflow, and that retrieval functions return correct values for real config blocks, to validate all acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 24
  }
}

